---
// Privacy. Copy: advisory_based_specs/02_Replacement_Copy.md §18, with the
// bracketed items completed from the owner's answers on 2026-09-27:
//   - Inbound email: ImprovMX (forwarding, per the public MX records), stored
//     in a personal Gmail account (Google).
//   - No client material in public AI services such as ChatGPT or Claude.
//   - Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled (owner confirmed; not visible in
//     this repo, because it is switched on in the Cloudflare dashboard).
//   - Operator stays under the PainToBuild name with the email address.
//   - No fixed retention period was chosen; deletion is on request.
// Update the review date below only when the page is actually reviewed.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Kicker from '../components/content/Kicker.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/routes';

const title = 'Privacy and your information | PainToBuild';
const description = 'Learn how PainToBuild handles messages, client information, email subscriptions and purchases, and how to ask questions about your information.';
const lastReviewed = { iso: '2026-09-27', label: 'September 27, 2026' };
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImagePath="/open-graph/privacy.png">
  <section class="wrap section prose">
    <Kicker>Privacy</Kicker>
    <h1>Privacy and your information</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page explains what happens to your information when you contact me, request a guide or
      pay for a review.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      PainToBuild is run by one person under the PainToBuild name. You can send privacy questions
      to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Messages and review material</h2>
    <p>
      When you email me, I receive your address, message and anything you attach. I use this
      information to reply and, if agreed, carry out the review.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email sent to {EMAIL} passes through ImprovMX, a service that forwards it to my inbox. It is
      then stored in my Gmail account, which Google provides. I do not share your messages or
      review material with other people unless you agree.
    </p>
    <p>You can ask me to delete your messages and review material at any time.</p>
    <p>Start with a short summary. I will ask for more information only if it is needed for the agreed work.</p>

    <h2>AI tools and other services</h2>
    <p>
      I do not put your messages or review material into public AI services, such as ChatGPT or
      Claude.
    </p>
    <p>
      The outside services that handle your information are the ones named on this page: ImprovMX
      and Google for email, MailerLite for template emails, Gumroad for guide purchases and
      Cloudflare for the website.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing examples of client work</h2>
    <p>
      I ask for separate permission before publishing your material or results. That permission
      covers what I can share and whether I can identify you.
    </p>

    <h2>Resource emails</h2>
    <p>
      The template request uses MailerLite to confirm your address and send the download. You also
      receive occasional updates, as explained when you sign up. You can unsubscribe through the
      link in an email.
    </p>
    <p>
      MailerLite keeps your address while you are subscribed. To have it removed completely, email
      {" "}<a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Gumroad handles payments for the guides and tools. Its checkout has its own terms and privacy
      information.
    </p>
    <p>
      As the seller, I can see the purchase details Gumroad shows sellers, such as your email
      address and what you bought. I never see your card details. For a personal review, how you
      pay is set out in your written agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Website visitor information</h2>
    <p>
      The website is served by Cloudflare. I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see which pages are
      read and roughly where visitors come from. It does not use cookies and does not follow you
      across other websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions or requests</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> if you have a question or want to ask about
      your information. You can ask what I hold about you, ask me to correct it or ask me to delete
      it. Depending on where you live, you may have other rights too.
    </p>

    <p class="reviewed">Last reviewed <time datetime={lastReviewed.iso}>{lastReviewed.label}</time>.</p>

    <ul class="link-list">
      <li><a href="/contact/">Contact me</a></li>
      <li><a href="/terms/">Terms</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section { padding-block: var(--s7) var(--s8); }
  .reviewed { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t-caption); margin-top: var(--s7) !important; }
</style>
